<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hamel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hamel was fought on 4 July 1918 near Le Hamel on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">Somme</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Planned by Sir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-monash">John Monash</a>, the Australian Corps, with American infantry, British tanks and aircraft, captured its objectives in about 93 minutes. The carefully coordinated attack became a model for the Allied offensive at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Amiens</a> a month later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hamel.jpg" alt="Battle of Hamel" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer : ? · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamel_(AWM_E02690).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
